Subject: [PATCH 07217/11362] [outer-loop] Prepare submission package with
 REQ-35's graduated fixes (kernel v9)

Ran the standing prep_daily_submission.py routine: refreshed the
iancblenke/carnot-agent-code dataset from the repo's current python/carnot
(now including REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-35's graduated fixes -- default-on
stall-refactor-loop, max_tokens/timeout 4096/600, structural reminder),
re-pushed the submission kernel (v9), and validated the save-run.

All safety guards passed: MAX_ACTIONS=400 present, no leaked _rust.so,
and a real import+build smoke test of the graduated agent code in the
staged bundle. The script's own 24x15s poll exited before the kernel
genuinely finished (Kaggle notebook runs took longer this time); manually
polled kernels status to KernelWorkerStatus.COMPLETE and confirmed
submission.parquet present via `kaggle kernels output` before correcting
the status file to reflect ground truth.

This does NOT submit to the competition -- per Operator-Only External
Publication discipline, that remains an explicit operator decision via
the printed --submit-only command.

